<style>
  /* Answers are printed upside down so the reader can choose when to peek. */
  .reveal { display: inline-block; transform: rotate(180deg) translateY(-0.2em); line-height: 1; }
</style>

{% comment %} ---------- Content lists: one item per line, fields split by | , items split by ~~ ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% capture facts_raw %}
Honey never spoils. Archaeologists have found pots of honey in ancient Egyptian tombs that are over 3,000 years old and still perfectly edible. ~~
Octopuses have three hearts and blue blood. Two hearts pump blood to the gills and one to the rest of the body. ~~
Botanically, bananas are berries but strawberries are not. ~~
A day on Venus is longer than its year. Venus takes 243 Earth days to spin once but only 225 to orbit the Sun. ~~
The Eiffel Tower grows about 15 centimetres taller in summer as the iron expands in the heat. ~~
Wombats are the only animals known to produce cube-shaped droppings. ~~
There are more possible games of chess than there are atoms in the observable universe. ~~
The national animal of Scotland is the unicorn. ~~
Sharks are older than trees. Sharks appeared around 450 million years ago, trees around 385 million. ~~
Cleopatra lived closer in time to the Moon landing than to the building of the Great Pyramid of Giza.
{% endcapture %}

{% capture trivia_raw %}
Science & nature|Which planet in our solar system has the most known moons?|Saturn ~~
Geography|What is the capital city of Australia?|Canberra ~~
History|In which year did the Berlin Wall fall?|1989 ~~
Science & nature|What is the chemical symbol for gold?|Au ~~
Art & literature|Who painted the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel?|Michelangelo ~~
Geography|Which is the longest river in Africa?|Nile ~~
Science & nature|How many bones are in the adult human body?|206 ~~
Music|Which composer wrote the Moonlight Sonata?|Beethoven ~~
Sport|How many players does a volleyball team have on court?|6 ~~
History|Who was the first person to walk on the Moon?|Neil Armstrong
{% endcapture %}

{% capture riddles_raw %}
I speak without a mouth and hear without ears. I have no body, but I come alive with the wind. What am I?|An echo ~~
What has keys but cannot open locks?|A piano ~~
The more you take, the more you leave behind. What am I?|Footsteps ~~
What has to be broken before you can use it?|An egg ~~
What gets wetter the more it dries?|A towel ~~
I have cities but no houses, forests but no trees, and water but no fish. What am I?|A map ~~
What can travel around the world while staying in a corner?|A stamp ~~
What has a head and a tail but no body?|A coin ~~
What runs but never walks, and has a mouth but never talks?|A river ~~
What goes up but never comes down?|Your age
{% endcapture %}

{% comment %} ---------- Pick today's items (local day of year, offset so the three lists don't move in lockstep) ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% assign local_ts = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | plus: trmnl.user.utc_offset %}
{% assign day_of_year = local_ts | date: "%j" | plus: 0 %}
{% assign now_hm = local_ts | date: "%H:%M" %}

{% assign facts = facts_raw | strip | split: "~~" %}
{% assign trivias = trivia_raw | strip | split: "~~" %}
{% assign riddles = riddles_raw | strip | split: "~~" %}
{% assign facts_count = facts | size %}
{% assign trivias_count = trivias | size %}
{% assign riddles_count = riddles | size %}

{% assign fact_idx = day_of_year | modulo: facts_count %}
{% assign trivia_idx = day_of_year | plus: 3 | modulo: trivias_count %}
{% assign riddle_idx = day_of_year | plus: 6 | modulo: riddles_count %}

{% assign fact_text = facts[fact_idx] | strip %}

{% assign trivia_parts = trivias[trivia_idx] | strip | split: "|" %}
{% assign trivia_category = trivia_parts[0] | strip %}
{% assign trivia_question = trivia_parts[1] | strip %}
{% assign trivia_answer = trivia_parts[2] | strip %}

{% assign riddle_parts = riddles[riddle_idx] | strip | split: "|" %}
{% assign riddle_question = riddle_parts[0] | strip %}
{% assign riddle_answer = riddle_parts[1] | strip %}

{% comment %} ---------- Polled data wins over the bundled samples above.
   data.json (built daily by scripts/build_data.py) has days["YYYY-MM-DD"] = { fact, trivia, riddle }. ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% assign today_key = local_ts | date: "%Y-%m-%d" %}
{% assign today_data = days[today_key] %}
{% assign data_source = "sample" %}
{% assign fact_label = "Did you know?" %}
{% if today_data %}
  {% assign data_source = "feed" %}
  {% if today_data.fact.text != blank %}
    {% assign fact_text = today_data.fact.text %}
    {% assign fact_url = today_data.fact.url %}
    {% if today_data.fact.kind == "on_this_day" %}{% assign fact_label = "On this day" %}{% endif %}
    {% if today_data.fact.kind == "misconception" %}{% assign fact_label = "Myth busted" %}{% endif %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if today_data.trivia.question != blank %}
    {% assign trivia_category = today_data.trivia.category %}
    {% assign trivia_question = today_data.trivia.question %}
    {% assign trivia_answer = today_data.trivia.answer %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if today_data.riddle.question != blank %}
    {% assign riddle_question = today_data.riddle.question %}
    {% assign riddle_answer = today_data.riddle.answer %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ---------- Resolve the answer display setting into one state: shown | upside_down | hidden | pending ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} Custom field values live under trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values; the hosted service also exposes them top-level. {% endcomment %}
{% assign cf = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values %}
{% assign answer_mode_value = cf.answer_mode | default: answer_mode | default: "upside_down" %}
{% assign reveal_time_value = cf.reveal_time | default: reveal_time | default: "" | slice: 0, 5 %}

{% assign answer_state = answer_mode_value %}
{% unless answer_state == "upside_down" or answer_state == "reveal_at_time" or answer_state == "shown" or answer_state == "hidden" %}{% assign answer_state = "upside_down" %}{% endunless %}
{% assign reveal_label = "" %}
{% if answer_state == "reveal_at_time" %}
  {% if reveal_time_value == blank or now_hm >= reveal_time_value %}
    {% assign answer_state = "shown" %}
  {% else %}
    {% assign answer_state = "pending" %}
    {% assign reveal_label = "2000-01-01 " | append: reveal_time_value | date: "%-I:%M %p" %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} ---------- Which sections are on (boolean custom fields; default on) ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% assign v = cf.show_fact %}{% if v == nil %}{% assign v = show_fact %}{% endif %}
{% assign fact_on = true %}{% if v == false or v == "false" or v == 0 or v == "0" %}{% assign fact_on = false %}{% endif %}
{% assign v = cf.show_trivia %}{% if v == nil %}{% assign v = show_trivia %}{% endif %}
{% assign trivia_on = true %}{% if v == false or v == "false" or v == 0 or v == "0" %}{% assign trivia_on = false %}{% endif %}
{% assign v = cf.show_riddle %}{% if v == nil %}{% assign v = show_riddle %}{% endif %}
{% assign riddle_on = true %}{% if v == false or v == "false" or v == 0 or v == "0" %}{% assign riddle_on = false %}{% endif %}
{% unless fact_on or trivia_on or riddle_on %}{% assign fact_on = true %}{% endunless %}

{% comment %} ---------- Slots: the hero is the user's chosen primary section if it is enabled, else the first enabled one (fact, trivia, riddle); the rest go to the sidebar in that same order. ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% assign primary_value = cf.primary | default: primary | default: "fact" %}
{% assign hero = "" %}
{% if primary_value == "fact" and fact_on %}{% assign hero = "fact" %}
{% elsif primary_value == "trivia" and trivia_on %}{% assign hero = "trivia" %}
{% elsif primary_value == "riddle" and riddle_on %}{% assign hero = "riddle" %}
{% elsif fact_on %}{% assign hero = "fact" %}
{% elsif trivia_on %}{% assign hero = "trivia" %}
{% else %}{% assign hero = "riddle" %}{% endif %}
{% assign sides = "" %}
{% if fact_on and hero != "fact" %}{% assign sides = sides | append: "fact," %}{% endif %}
{% if trivia_on and hero != "trivia" %}{% assign sides = sides | append: "trivia," %}{% endif %}
{% if riddle_on and hero != "riddle" %}{% assign sides = sides | append: "riddle," %}{% endif %}
{% assign sides = sides | split: "," %}
{% assign side_count = sides | size %}
{% assign side1 = sides[0] %}
{% assign side2 = sides[1] %}

{% comment %} Per-slot content, so layouts only ever pass slot variables. {% endcomment %}
{% case hero %}
  {% when "fact" %}{% assign hero_label = fact_label %}{% assign hero_body = fact_text %}{% assign hero_answer = "" %}
  {% when "riddle" %}{% assign hero_label = "Riddle me this" %}{% assign hero_body = riddle_question %}{% assign hero_answer = riddle_answer %}
  {% else %}{% assign hero_label = "Trivia · " | append: trivia_category %}{% assign hero_body = trivia_question %}{% assign hero_answer = trivia_answer %}
{% endcase %}
{% case side1 %}
  {% when "fact" %}{% assign side1_label = fact_label %}{% assign side1_body = fact_text %}{% assign side1_answer = "" %}
  {% when "trivia" %}{% assign side1_label = "Trivia · " | append: trivia_category %}{% assign side1_body = trivia_question %}{% assign side1_answer = trivia_answer %}
  {% when "riddle" %}{% assign side1_label = "Riddle me this" %}{% assign side1_body = riddle_question %}{% assign side1_answer = riddle_answer %}
{% endcase %}
{% case side2 %}
  {% when "trivia" %}{% assign side2_label = "Trivia · " | append: trivia_category %}{% assign side2_body = trivia_question %}{% assign side2_answer = trivia_answer %}
  {% when "riddle" %}{% assign side2_label = "Riddle me this" %}{% assign side2_body = riddle_question %}{% assign side2_answer = riddle_answer %}
{% endcase %}

{% comment %} Short labels for the narrow quadrant columns, where "Trivia · Science & nature · Answer: …" would wrap. {% endcomment %}
{% case side1 %}{% when "fact" %}{% assign side1_short = fact_label %}{% when "trivia" %}{% assign side1_short = "Trivia" %}{% else %}{% assign side1_short = "Riddle" %}{% endcase %}
{% case side2 %}{% when "trivia" %}{% assign side2_short = "Trivia" %}{% else %}{% assign side2_short = "Riddle" %}{% endcase %}

{% comment %} Title bar instance text reflects what is enabled. {% endcomment %}
{% assign instance_label = "Daily Brain Snack" %}
{% unless fact_on and trivia_on and riddle_on %}
  {% assign names = "" %}
  {% if fact_on %}{% assign names = names | append: "Fact," %}{% endif %}
  {% if trivia_on %}{% assign names = names | append: "Trivia," %}{% endif %}
  {% if riddle_on %}{% assign names = names | append: "Riddle," %}{% endif %}
  {% assign instance_label = names | split: "," | join: " & " | capitalize %}
{% endunless %}

{% comment %} ---------- Templates ---------- {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} One step up the size ladder; used for the lg (TRMNL X) variants. {% endcomment %}
{% template size_up %}{% case size %}{% when "small" %}base{% when "base" %}large{% when "large" %}xlarge{% else %}xxlarge{% endcase %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} The answer (or the reveal time) goes on the label line so it never costs a body line. {% endcomment %}
{% template with_answer %}{% if answer != blank %}{% case state %}{% when "shown" %}{{ label }} · Answer: {{ answer }}{% when "upside_down" %}{{ label }} · Answer:&nbsp;<span class="reveal">{{ answer }}</span>{% when "pending" %}{{ label }} · After {{ reveal_label }}{% else %}{{ label }}{% endcase %}{% else %}{{ label }}{% endif %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Hero slot: filled label, big text, answer (if any).
   lines is the OG clamp; lg_lines the TRMNL X clamp (defaults to lines). Text steps up one size on lg. {% endcomment %}
{% template hero_card %}
{% capture lg_size %}{% render "size_up", size: title_size %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign lg_clamp = lg_lines | default: lines %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left flex--top gap--small">
  <span class="label label--filled lg:label--large">{% render "with_answer", label: label, answer: answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label %}</span>
  <span class="title title--{{ title_size }} lg:title--{{ lg_size }}" data-clamp="{{ lines }}" data-clamp-lg="{{ lg_clamp }}">{{ body }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Sidebar slot: underlined label, question, answer. body_class is one of description / title title--small / title / title title--large. {% endcomment %}
{% template side_card %}
{% capture lg_label %}{% render "size_up", size: label_size %}{% endcapture %}
{% case body_class %}
  {% when "description" %}{% assign lg_body = "lg:title--small" %}
  {% when "title title--small" %}{% assign lg_body = "lg:title--base" %}
  {% when "title" %}{% assign lg_body = "lg:title--large" %}
  {% else %}{% assign lg_body = "lg:title--xlarge" %}
{% endcase %}
{% assign lg_clamp = lg_lines | default: lines %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left flex--top gap--xsmall">
  <span class="label label--{{ label_size }} lg:label--{{ lg_label }} label--underline">{% render "with_answer", label: label, answer: answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label %}</span>
  <span class="{{ body_class }} {{ lg_body }}" data-clamp="{{ lines }}" data-clamp-lg="{{ lg_clamp }}">{{ body }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ---------- Space budgets: short cards donate their unused room to long ones. ----------
   Each layout passes the measured pixel room for body text (with no answer lines shown) as `room` (OG) and `room_lg`
   (TRMNL X). Cards are given clamps by how much of that room they need. Metrics below were measured in the browser.
   cpl: characters per line for a text size at a content width (glyph width x 1.15 for wrap waste; near enough on X too).
   lh: line height of a text size per device (dev = og | lg). {% endcomment %}
{% template cpl %}{% case size %}{% when "description" %}{{ width | times: 10 | divided_by: 69 }}{% when "small" %}{{ width | times: 10 | divided_by: 92 }}{% when "base" %}{{ width | divided_by: 12 }}{% when "large" %}{{ width | times: 10 | divided_by: 152 }}{% when "xlarge" %}{{ width | times: 10 | divided_by: 175 }}{% else %}{{ width | times: 10 | divided_by: 198 }}{% endcase %}{% endtemplate %}
{% template lh %}{% if dev == "lg" %}{% case size %}{% when "description" %}19{% when "small" %}25{% when "base" %}36{% when "large" %}42{% else %}48{% endcase %}{% else %}{% case size %}{% when "description" %}12{% when "small" %}16{% when "base" %}21{% when "large" %}36{% when "xlarge" %}42{% else %}48{% endcase %}{% endif %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} lines_needed: ceil(chars / cpl), 0 for empty text. {% endcomment %}
{% template lines_needed %}{% assign chars = text | size %}{% if chars == 0 %}0{% else %}{{ chars | plus: cpl | minus: 1 | divided_by: cpl }}{% endif %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} fit3: share a budget between three cards given what each needs (any unit). Outputs "h,s1,s2".
   If everything fits, each card gets its need plus the slack (clamps are only a ceiling). Otherwise cards
   within their fair share keep their need and the long ones split what is left. {% endcomment %}
{% template fit3 %}
{% assign sum = need_h | plus: need_1 | plus: need_2 %}
{% if sum <= budget %}
  {% assign slack = budget | minus: sum %}
  {{ need_h | plus: slack }},{{ need_1 | plus: slack }},{{ need_2 | plus: slack }}
{% else %}
  {% assign n = 0 %}
  {% if need_h > 0 %}{% assign n = n | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_1 > 0 %}{% assign n = n | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_2 > 0 %}{% assign n = n | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% assign share = budget | divided_by: n %}
  {% assign small = 0 %}{% assign big = 0 %}
  {% if need_h <= share %}{% assign small = small | plus: need_h %}{% else %}{% assign big = big | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_1 <= share %}{% assign small = small | plus: need_1 %}{% else %}{% assign big = big | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_2 <= share %}{% assign small = small | plus: need_2 %}{% else %}{% assign big = big | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
  {% assign rem = budget | minus: small %}
  {% assign each = rem | divided_by: big %}
  {% assign used = each | times: big %}
  {% assign extra = rem | minus: used %}
  {% if need_h <= share %}{{ need_h }}{% else %}{{ each | plus: extra }}{% assign extra = 0 %}{% endif %},{% if need_1 <= share %}{{ need_1 }}{% else %}{{ each | plus: extra }}{% assign extra = 0 %}{% endif %},{% if need_2 <= share %}{{ need_2 }}{% else %}{{ each | plus: extra }}{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} alloc3: line clamps for hero / side1 / side2 given each text, the sizes, content width(s), a pixel budget and the device. Outputs "h,s1,s2". {% endcomment %}
{% template alloc3 %}
{% assign hero_width = hero_width | default: width %}
{% capture cpl_h %}{% render "cpl", size: hero_size, width: hero_width %}{% endcapture %}{% assign cpl_h = cpl_h | strip | plus: 0 %}
{% capture cpl_s %}{% render "cpl", size: side_size, width: width %}{% endcapture %}{% assign cpl_s = cpl_s | strip | plus: 0 %}
{% capture lh_h %}{% render "lh", size: hero_size, dev: dev %}{% endcapture %}{% assign lh_h = lh_h | strip | plus: 0 %}
{% capture lh_s %}{% render "lh", size: side_size, dev: dev %}{% endcapture %}{% assign lh_s = lh_s | strip | plus: 0 %}
{% capture need_h %}{% render "lines_needed", text: hero_body, cpl: cpl_h %}{% endcapture %}{% assign need_h = need_h | strip | times: lh_h %}
{% capture need_1 %}{% render "lines_needed", text: side1_body, cpl: cpl_s %}{% endcapture %}{% assign need_1 = need_1 | strip | times: lh_s %}
{% capture need_2 %}{% render "lines_needed", text: side2_body, cpl: cpl_s %}{% endcapture %}{% assign need_2 = need_2 | strip | times: lh_s %}
{% capture px %}{% render "fit3", need_h: need_h, need_1: need_1, need_2: need_2, budget: budget %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign px = px | strip | split: "," %}
{% assign l_h = px[0] | plus: 0 | divided_by: lh_h %}
{% assign l_1 = px[1] | plus: 0 | divided_by: lh_s %}
{% assign l_2 = px[2] | plus: 0 | divided_by: lh_s %}
{% comment %} Rounding down to whole lines can leave room unused; hand it back, one line at a time, to cards that are still clipped. {% endcomment %}
{% assign used_h = l_h | times: lh_h %}{% assign used_1 = l_1 | times: lh_s %}{% assign used_2 = l_2 | times: lh_s %}
{% assign left = budget | minus: used_h | minus: used_1 | minus: used_2 %}
{% for i in (1..3) %}
  {% if need_h > used_h and left >= lh_h %}{% assign l_h = l_h | plus: 1 %}{% assign used_h = used_h | plus: lh_h %}{% assign left = left | minus: lh_h %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_1 > used_1 and left >= lh_s %}{% assign l_1 = l_1 | plus: 1 %}{% assign used_1 = used_1 | plus: lh_s %}{% assign left = left | minus: lh_s %}{% endif %}
  {% if need_2 > used_2 and left >= lh_s %}{% assign l_2 = l_2 | plus: 1 %}{% assign used_2 = used_2 | plus: lh_s %}{% assign left = left | minus: lh_s %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{{ l_h }},{{ l_1 }},{{ l_2 }}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} body_class (description / title title--small / title / title title--large) -> size name. {% endcomment %}
{% template body_size %}{% case body_class %}{% when "description" %}description{% when "title title--small" %}small{% when "title" %}base{% when "title title--large" %}large{% else %}xlarge{% endcase %}{% endtemplate %}



{% comment %} Stacked layout (hero on top, sides below): used by the narrow/tall views and every portrait variant.
   hidden: extra classes for the wrapper (e.g. landscape:hidden). room / room_lg: measured body-text room in px with
   all three sections on; each missing side gives its label and divider back. {% endcomment %}
{% template stacked %}
{% assign width = width | default: 385 %}
{% if side_count < 1 %}{% assign side1_body = "" %}{% assign side1_answer = "" %}{% endif %}
{% if side_count < 2 %}{% assign side2_body = "" %}{% assign side2_answer = "" %}{% endif %}
{% capture s_size %}{% render "body_size", body_class: side_body %}{% endcapture %}{% assign s_size = s_size | strip %}
{% assign missing = 2 | minus: side_count %}
{% assign budget = missing | times: 34 | plus: room %}
{% assign budget_lg = missing | times: 45 | plus: room_lg %}
{% capture alloc %}{% render "alloc3", hero_body: hero_body, side1_body: side1_body, side2_body: side2_body, hero_size: hero_size, side_size: s_size, width: width, budget: budget, dev: "og" %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign alloc = alloc | strip | split: "," %}
{% capture alloc_lg %}{% render "alloc3", hero_body: hero_body, side1_body: side1_body, side2_body: side2_body, hero_size: hero_size, side_size: s_size, width: width, budget: budget_lg, dev: "lg" %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign alloc_lg = alloc_lg | strip | split: "," %}
<div class="layout layout--col layout--top layout--stretch-x gap--{{ gap }} {{ hidden }}">
  {% render "hero_card", label: hero_label, body: hero_body, answer: hero_answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label, title_size: hero_size, text_size: hero_text, lines: alloc[0], lg_lines: alloc_lg[0] %}
  {% if side_count > 0 %}
  <div class="divider divider--h"></div>
  {% render "side_card", label: side1_label, body: side1_body, answer: side1_answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label, label_size: side_label, body_class: side_body, text_size: side_text, lines: alloc[1], lg_lines: alloc_lg[1] %}
  {% endif %}
  {% if side_count > 1 %}
  <div class="divider divider--h"></div>
  {% render "side_card", label: side2_label, body: side2_body, answer: side2_answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label, label_size: side_label, body_class: side_body, text_size: side_text, lines: alloc[2], lg_lines: alloc_lg[2] %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Two side cards stacked in their own column (half_horizontal and full landscape sidebars, TRMNL X quadrant rows):
   room / room_lg is the measured body-text room of that column. {% endcomment %}
{% template side_pair %}
{% assign width = width | default: 380 %}
{% capture s_size %}{% render "body_size", body_class: side_body %}{% endcapture %}{% assign s_size = s_size | strip %}
{% assign budget = room %}
{% assign budget_lg = room_lg %}
{% capture alloc %}{% render "alloc3", hero_body: "", side1_body: side1_body, side2_body: side2_body, hero_size: "small", side_size: s_size, width: width, budget: budget, dev: "og" %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign alloc = alloc | strip | split: "," %}
{% capture alloc_lg %}{% render "alloc3", hero_body: "", side1_body: side1_body, side2_body: side2_body, hero_size: "small", side_size: s_size, width: width, budget: budget_lg, dev: "lg" %}{% endcapture %}
{% assign alloc_lg = alloc_lg | strip | split: "," %}
{% render "side_card", label: side1_label, body: side1_body, answer: side1_answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label, label_size: side_label, body_class: side_body, text_size: side_text, lines: alloc[1], lg_lines: alloc_lg[1] %}
<div class="divider divider--h"></div>
{% render "side_card", label: side2_label, body: side2_body, answer: side2_answer, state: state, reveal_label: reveal_label, label_size: side_label, body_class: side_body, text_size: side_text, lines: alloc[2], lg_lines: alloc_lg[2] %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% template plugin_title_bar %}
<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image image--adaptive" alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;utf8,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='32' height='32' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='14' fill='none' stroke='%23000' stroke-width='3'/%3E%3Ctext x='16' y='23' font-family='Arial, sans-serif' font-size='20' font-weight='bold' text-anchor='middle' fill='%23000'%3E?%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E">
  <span class="title">Facts, Trivia &amp; Riddles</span>
  {% if instance != blank %}<span class="instance">{{ instance }}</span>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
